mesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/colorado-city-uses-15-minute-water-data-from-smart-meters-to-catch-illegal-lawn-watering-during-drought/articleshow/133203136.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/colorado-city-uses-15-minute-water-data-from-smart-meters-to-catch-illegal-lawn-watering-during-drought/articleshow/133203136.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T13:07:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133203136,imgsize-235225.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[73 years later, Cape Cod removes barrier blocking native trout’s return]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133187994.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1953-construction-narrowed-cape-cods-fresh-brook-a-concrete-weir-then-blocked-sea-run-brook-trout-from-their-spawning-grounds-and-73-years-later-it-is-set-to-be-removed-to-bring-the-native-trout-back/articleshow/133187994.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1953-construction-narrowed-cape-cods-fresh-brook-a-concrete-weir-then-blocked-sea-run-brook-trout-from-their-spawning-grounds-and-73-years-later-it-is-set-to-be-removed-to-bring-the-native-trout-back/articleshow/133187994.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T13:01:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133188184,imgsize-153622.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[If vivid dreams leave you exhausted, experts say the problem may not be the dreams but disruptions that prevent deep sleep]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133202430.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Feeling fatigued after dreaming is often linked to disrupted sleep patterns, especially during REM phases. During REM, the brain remains highly engaged, which prevents achieving deeper rest. If dreams are recalled, it signals that you woke while dreaming, interrupting the crucial restorative stages of sleep. This interference obstructs clearing adenosine, a natural sleep-inducing byproduct, making tiredness arise from your awakening moment rather than the dreams themselves.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/most-dreaming-happens-during-rem-sleep-which-makes-up-2025-of-the-night-if-vivid-dreams-keep-leaving-you-exhausted-scientists-say-the-real-culprit-may-be-something-else-keeping-you-from-restorative-sleep/articleshow/133202430.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/most-dreaming-happens-during-rem-sleep-which-makes-up-2025-of-the-night-if-vivid-dreams-keep-leaving-you-exhausted-scientists-say-the-real-culprit-may-be-something-else-keeping-you-from-restorative-sleep/articleshow/133202430.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T13:00:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133202706,imgsize-114000.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why is ICE under fire over its $20 million electric shock-glove plan?]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133200753.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/why-is-ice-under-fire-over-its-20-million-electric-shock-glove-plan/articleshow/133200753.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/why-is-ice-under-fire-over-its-20-million-electric-shock-glove-plan/articleshow/133200753.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T12:36:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133203179,imgsize-107700.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[More than 99% of California’s sunflower sea stars vanished, now scientists have found a mysterious colony that could help revive dying kelp forests]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133200597.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ten years ago, sunflower sea stars faced near extinction due to a devastating marine epidemic, leading to unchecked sea urchin populations that destroyed essential kelp forests. Recently, a newly identified colony of these sea stars has rekindled hope for ecological restoration. Researchers are examining their resilience to diseases, which could greatly benefit efforts to reintroduce these vital predators to their ocean habitats.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/more-than-99-of-californias-sunflower-sea-stars-vanished-now-scientists-have-found-a-mysterious-colony-that-could-help-revive-dying-kelp-forests/articleshow/133200597.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/more-than-99-of-californias-sunflower-sea-stars-vanished-now-scientists-have-found-a-mysterious-colony-that-could-help-revive-dying-kelp-forests/articleshow/133200597.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T12:02:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133200760,imgsize-137685.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Minnesota church closes after 70 years, gives $600,000 to nonprofits and supports housing]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133160367.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[St. Mark's United Church of Christ closed after seven decades due to declining membership.  The congregation distributed approximately $600,000 among 21 local nonprofits.  A substantial gift of $115,000 went to Loaves &amp; Fishes for meal provision.  The church property will be redeveloped into affordable housing units for the community.  This act ensures the church's legacy continues through support and new homes.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/one-last-act-of-kindness-a-minnesota-church-closed-after-its-congregation-fell-to-26-members-then-gave-about-600000-to-nonprofits-and-sold-its-property-for-affordable-housing/articleshow/133160367.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/one-last-act-of-kindness-a-minnesota-church-closed-after-its-congregation-fell-to-26-members-then-gave-about-600000-to-nonprofits-and-sold-its-property-for-affordable-housing/articleshow/133160367.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T12:10:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133160671,imgsize-718369.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ireland’s vanished rainforest is getting a second chance with 30,000 trees]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133199605.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/irelands-ancient-rainforest-vanished-after-thousands-of-years-of-human-activity-now-nearly-30000-trees-are-being-planted-to-bring-it-back/articleshow/133199605.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/irelands-ancient-rainforest-vanished-after-thousands-of-years-of-human-activity-now-nearly-30000-trees-are-being-planted-to-bring-it-back/articleshow/133199605.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T12:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133200166,imgsize-247985.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australian family turns remote sheep farm island into $4.8m wildlife haven]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133199043.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australian-family-bought-a-remote-island-to-run-a-sheep-farm-now-they-are-turning-it-into-a-4-8-million-conservation-sanctuary-for-endangered-wildlife/articleshow/133199043.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australian-family-bought-a-remote-island-to-run-a-sheep-farm-now-they-are-turning-it-into-a-4-8-million-conservation-sanctuary-for-endangered-wildlife/articleshow/133199043.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T11:31:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133203854,imgsize-1200306.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why Putin’s first Kuril Islands visit matters as Russia-Japan ties hit new low]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133198569.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Russian President Vladimir Putin visited the disputed Kuril Islands for the first time.  This visit occurred amid deeply strained relations between Russia and Japan.  Japan strongly protests the visit, reiterating its territorial claims over the islands.  The long-standing dispute has intensified since Russia's invasion of Ukraine.  This territorial disagreement prevents a formal World War II peace treaty.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/why-putins-first-kuril-islands-visit-matters-as-russia-japan-ties-hit-new-low/articleshow/133198569.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/why-putins-first-kuril-islands-visit-matters-as-russia-japan-ties-hit-new-low/articleshow/133198569.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T11:03:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133199199,imgsize-64526.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[280,000 trees transform New Zealand island into conservation sanctuary]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133161170.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/how-280000-volunteer-planted-trees-transformed-new-zealands-tiritiri-matangi-from-a-degraded-island-into-a-conservation-sanctuary/articleshow/133161170.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/how-280000-volunteer-planted-trees-transformed-new-zealands-tiritiri-matangi-from-a-degraded-island-into-a-conservation-sanctuary/articleshow/133161170.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T11:05:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133161296,imgsize-250248.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Dogs can read human emotions! Scientists want you to smile]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133177993.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[New research confirms dogs can differentiate human emotions through facial expressions.  Their brains process happy faces in a unique reward region, showing emotional significance.  Dogs also distinguish between fear, anger, and sadness with distinct brain activity patterns.  This ability developed through domestication, aiding their social understanding of humans.  Understanding these emotions does not mean dogs experience them identically to people.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/dog-parents-you-were-right-all-along-scientists-finally-find-dogs-can-tell-when-youre-sad-scared-or-angry-heres-why-they-want-you-to-smile/articleshow/133177993.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/dog-parents-you-were-right-all-along-scientists-finally-find-dogs-can-tell-when-youre-sad-scared-or-angry-heres-why-they-want-you-to-smile/articleshow/133177993.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-12T15:40:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133178114,imgsize-209075.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Leavitt to leave White House podium to become MAGA warrior mom]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133198708.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/leavitt-to-leave-white-house-podium-to-become-maga-warrior-mom/articleshow/133198708.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/leavitt-to-leave-white-house-podium-to-become-maga-warrior-mom/articleshow/133198708.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T10:46:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Chidanand Rajghatta</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133198741,imgsize-82678.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Potatoes 'boiling' in ground, l